Task 1: Order Confirmation Generator

Write a Dart console program that takes food order details and prints a formatted confirmation message with a delivery tier and order 
status label.

->Declare variables for order ID (int), customer name (String), number of items (int) and total amount (double) with realistic sample 
values.
->Use string interpolation to print a formatted order confirmation that includes all four values in a readable message.
->Use an if-else statement to print the delivery tier: 'Express Delivery' if the total amount exceeds Rs 500 otherwise 'Standard 
Delivery'.
->Use a switch statement to print a status label based on a status code variable: 'Preparing' for 1,'Out for Delivery' for 2, 
'Delivered' for 3.

void main() 
{
  int orderId = 101;
  String customerName = "Rushita";
  int numberOfItems = 3;
  double totalAmount = 650.0;
  int statusCode = 1;

  // Order Confirmation
  print("===== Order Confirmation =====");
  print("Order ID: $orderId");
  print("Customer Name: $customerName");
  print("Number of Items: $numberOfItems");
  print("Total Amount: Rs. $totalAmount");

  // Delivery Tier
  if (totalAmount > 500) {
    print("Delivery Tier: Express Delivery");
  } else {
    print("Delivery Tier: Standard Delivery");
  }

  // Order Status
  switch (statusCode) {
    case 1:
      print("Order Status: Preparing");
      break;
    case 2:
      print("Order Status: Out for Delivery");
      break;
    case 3:
      print("Order Status: Delivered");
      break;
    default:
      print("Order Status: Invalid Status Code");
  }

  print("==============================");
}

